<title>USA: Becton Dickinson says govt allows merger.</title>
<headline>Becton Dickinson says govt allows merger.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKLIN LAKES, N.J. 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Becton Dickinson and Co said it has received government approvals for its previously announced acquisition of PharMingen.</p>
<p>Becton Dickinson said that the acquisition would broaden and enhance its flow cytometry business, Becton Dickinson Immunocytometry Systems, which is headquartered in San Jose, Calif.</p>
<p>PharMingen develops, manufactures and sells high-quality antibodies and reagents for immunology, cell biology and molecular biology research.  Becton Dickinson makes and sells medical supplies and devices and diagnostic systems.</p>
</text>
